  "emailBody": "\n        <html>\n\n        <body\n            style=\"\n                font-family:Segoe UI, Arial, sans-serif;\n                margin:20px;\n            \"\n        >\n\n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    background:#d42e12;\n                    color:white;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                \"\n            >\n\n\n               <h1 style=\"margin:0;\">\n                    Fuel Market Intelligence Morning Report\n                </h1>\n\n                <p style=\"margin:5px 0 0 0;\">\n                    21 August 2026\n                </p>\n\n            </div>\n\n            <p\n                style=\"\n                    font-size:16px;\n                    margin-top:20px;\n                    margin-bottom:20px;\n                \"\n            >\n                Good morning Sir,\n                <br><br>\n                \n                Here is today's fuel market intelligence report highlighting\n                the latest PMS and AGO depot prices together with key industry\n                developments and market news.\n            </p>\n\n            <br>\n\n            \n        <h2 style=\"color:#d42e12;\">\n            PMS Prices\n        </h2>\n\n        <div\n            style=\"\n                background:#fad5a1;\n                padding:12px;\n                border-left:5px solid #f28e05;\n                margin-bottom:10px;\n                font-size:16px;\n                font-weight:bold;\n            \"\n        >\n            Average PMS Prices: ₦1,203.12/L\n        </div>\n\n        <table\n            width=\"100%\"\n            cellspacing=\"0\"\n            cellpadding=\"10\"\n            style=\"\n                border-collapse:collapse;\n                border:1px solid #ddd;\n            \"\n        >\n\n            <tr style=\"background:#d42e12;color:white;\">\n                <th align=\"left\">Depot</th>\n                <th align=\"left\">Price</th>\n            </tr>\n\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>INTERGRATED</td>\n                <td>₦1,195.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>AFRICAN TERMINAL</td>\n                <td>₦1,195.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>RAINOIL DELTA</td>\n                <td>₦1,215.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>DANGOTE</td>\n                <td>₦1,185.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>PINNACLE</td>\n                <td>₦1,190.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>SIGMUND</td>\n                <td>₦1,215.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>TSL</td>\n                <td>₦1,215.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>LIQUID BULK</td>\n                <td>₦1,215.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n\n        </table>\n\n        <br>\n        \n\n            \n        <h2 style=\"color:#d42e12;\">\n            AGO Prices\n        </h2>\n\n        <div\n            style=\"\n                background:#fad5a1;\n                padding:12px;\n                border-left:5px solid #f28e05;\n                margin-bottom:10px;\n                font-size:16px;\n                font-weight:bold;\n            \"\n        >\n            Average AGO Prices: ₦1,740.62/L\n        </div>\n\n        <table\n            width=\"100%\"\n            cellspacing=\"0\"\n            cellpadding=\"10\"\n            style=\"\n                border-collapse:collapse;\n                border:1px solid #ddd;\n            \"\n        >\n\n            <tr style=\"background:#d42e12;color:white;\">\n                <th align=\"left\">Depot</th>\n                <th align=\"left\">Price</th>\n            </tr>\n\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>IBETO</td>\n                <td>₦1,660.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>IBACHEM</td>\n                <td>₦1,665.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>NIPCO WARRI</td>\n                <td>₦1,800.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>RAINOIL DELTA</td>\n                <td>₦1,850.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>ZAMSON</td>\n                <td>₦1,800.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>PRUDENT OGHARA</td>\n                <td>₦1,800.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>RAINOIL LAGOS</td>\n                <td>₦1,680.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>OBAT OIL</td>\n                <td>₦1,670.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n\n        </table>\n\n        <br>\n        \n\n            \n        <h2 style=\"color:#d42e12;\">\n            Market News\n        </h2>\n        \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Strait of Hormuz Crisis Drives Global EV Sales Higher as Oil Shock Persists\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Electric vehicles could account for about 25 per cent of the global vehicle fleet by 2040. Wood Mackenzie said faster EV adoption could have significant implications for the global oil industry. The resulting decline in road-transport fuel demand could force about 40 refineries worldwide to close earlier than previously expected.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/strait-of-hormuz-crisis-drives-global-ev-sales-higher-as-oil-shock-persists-2\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    BREAKING: Dangote Refinery Raises Petrol Gantry Price to ₦1,185/Litre\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Dangote Petroleum Refinery has raised its Premium Motor Spirit (PMS) gantry price by ₦20 per litre. The new price is effective midnight, August 21, 2026. The adjustment comes against a Lagos depot market where PMS is currently trading at ⁦1,200 perlitre.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/breaking-dangote-refinery-raises-petrol-gantry-price-to-1185litre\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Oil Prices Rise Nearly 3% as Trump Threatens Iran Backers\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    As of 11:30 a.m. WAT, Brent crude was trading at $93.82 per barrel, up $2.20 or 2.40% , while West Texas Intermediate (WTI) stood at $86.65 per barrel. The latest advance came after U.S. President Donald Trump announced what he described as the “most crushing economic operation” against Iran.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/oil-prices-rise-nearly-3-as-trump-threatens-iran-backers\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    BREAKING: Dangote Refinery Raises Diesel Price by ₦100 to ₦1,670/Litre\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    The Dangote Petroleum Refinery has increased its Automotive Gas Oil (AGO) price by ₦100 per litre. The increase comes amid a rise in international crude oil prices, with Brent crude recently trading above $93 per barrel.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/breaking-dangote-refinery-raises-diesel-price-by-100-to-1670litre\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Atiku Pledges to Restore Fuel Subsidy if Elected in 2027\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Former Vice President Atiku Abubakar has pledged to reinstate Nigeria’s fuel subsidy if he wins the presidency in the 2027 general election. Atiku, who is the presidential candidate of the African Democratic Congress (ADC), said he initially did not oppose the decision to remove the subsidy. The decision led to a sharp increase in petrol prices and contributed to higher transportation costs.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/atiku-pledges-to-restore-fuel-subsidy-if-elected-in-2027\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n\n        </body>\n\n        </html>\n        "
